=== icupkg ===
DESCRIPTION · preview ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Read the input ICU .dat package file, modify it according to the options,
swap it to the desired platform properties (charset & endianness), and
optionally write the resulting ICU .dat package to the output file. Items
are removed, then added, then extracted and listed. An ICU .dat package is
written if items are removed or added, or if the input and output filenames
differ, or if the --writepkg (-w) option is set.

If the input filename is "new" then an empty package is created. If the
output filename is missing, then it is automatically generated from the
input filename: If the input filename ends with an l, b, or e matching its
platform properties, then the output filename will contain the letter from
…
                                               ↓ full description at the end
USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  icupkg [-h|-?|--help ] [-tl|-tb|-te] [-c] [-C comment] [-a list] [-r list]
      [-x list] [-l [-o outputListFileName]] [-s path] [-d path] [-w] [-m
      mode] [--ignore-deps] [--auto_toc_prefix]
      [--auto_toc_prefix_with_type] [--toc_prefix] infilename [outfilename]


POSITIONALS (2) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  infilename
  outfilename


FLAGS (17) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-w, --writepkg           write the output package even if no items are
                         removed or added (e.g., for only swapping the data)
-m, --matchmode mode     set the matching mode for item names with wildcards
                         noslash: the '*' wildcard does not match the '/'
                         tree separator
    --ignore-deps        Do not fail if not all resource dependencies are
                         met. Use this option if the missing resources come
                         from another source.
    --auto_toc_prefix    automatic ToC entries prefix Uses the prefix of the
                         first entry of the input package, rather than its
                         basename. Requires a non-empty input package.
    --auto_toc_prefix_with_type auto_toc_prefix + adjust platform type Same
                         as auto_toc_prefix but also checks that the prefix
                         ends with the input platform type letter, and
                         modifies it to the output platform type letter. At
                         most one of the auto_toc_prefix options can be used
                         at a time.
    --toc_prefix prefix  ToC prefix to be used in the output package
                         Overrides the package basename and
                         --auto_toc_prefix. Cannot be combined with
                         --auto_toc_prefix_with_type.
-s, --sourcedir path     directory for the --add items
-d, --destdir path       directory for the --extract items
-l, --list               list the package items (after modifying the
                         package) to stdout or to output list file
-o, --outlist path       path/filename for the --list output

(Only the last occurrence of an option is used.) ───────────────────────────
-h, --help               print this message and exit
 or -?
-t, --type
                           values:
                             l  output for little-endian/ASCII charset
                                family
                             b  output for big-endian/ASCII charset family
                             e  output for big-endian/EBCDIC charset family
                                The output type defaults to the input type.
-c, --copyright          include the ICU copyright notice
-C, --comment comment    include a comment string
-a, --add list           add items to the package
-r, --remove list        remove items from the package
-x, --extract list       extract items from the package


DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Read the input ICU .dat package file, modify it according to the options,
swap it to the desired platform properties (charset & endianness), and
optionally write the resulting ICU .dat package to the output file. Items
are removed, then added, then extracted and listed. An ICU .dat package is
written if items are removed or added, or if the input and output filenames
differ, or if the --writepkg (-w) option is set.

If the input filename is "new" then an empty package is created. If the
output filename is missing, then it is automatically generated from the
input filename: If the input filename ends with an l, b, or e matching its
platform properties, then the output filename will contain the letter from
the -t (--type) option.

This tool can also be used to just swap a single ICU data file, replacing
the former icuswap tool. For this mode, provide the infilename (and optional
outfilename) for a non-package ICU data file. Allowed options include -t,
-w, -s and -d. The filenames can be absolute, or relative to the source/dest
dir paths. Other options are not allowed in this mode.
